---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ShareGroupMockup } from "../components/ShareGroupMockup";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Why this directory exists | Spokane List</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="One tap, no sign-up: share a Spokane contractor in a group chat with the name, number, and listing."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="how-it-works">
    <p class="hero-eyebrow">Why we’re here</p>
    <h1>Share a name that actually helps</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One tap. No sign-up. When a neighbor asks for a plumber, you paste a
      complete name—not a scavenger hunt.
    </p>

    <ShareGroupMockup origin="https://spokanelist.com" />

    <section>
      <h2>The usual thread</h2>
      <p>
        Someone drops a name from memory. Then the pile-on: what’s their number,
        do they have a site, can I see their work? You’re hunting Google and old
        posts instead of being helpful.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>One tap. No account.</h2>
      <p>
        Tap share. They get the name, trade, city, phone, website, and a listing
        link. You don’t create a login to browse, save, or send it. You still
        verify license and insurance before you hire.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>If you’re the contractor</h2>
      <p>
        Free listing. No second profile to manage. Keep your Google Business
        Profile current—when a neighbor shares you, they paste something complete
        instead of a screenshot.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="how-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href="/">Browse contractors</a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How sharing works</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
